---
/**
 * Privacy policy.
 *
 * Written from what the site actually does rather than from a template: every
 * third party named below is one this build genuinely loads or submits to —
 * the HighLevel forms and tracking script, Google Fonts, the Maps embeds, the
 * YouTube embeds in the members' nutrition course, the WhatsApp links, and
 * GitHub Pages as the host. If an embed is ever removed, the matching
 * paragraph should go with it.
 *
 * Indexable on purpose: a privacy policy people cannot find does not do its
 * job, and Google expects a business site to have one it can reach.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Schema from '../components/Schema.astro';
import { studios } from '../data/studios';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { url } from '../lib/url';

/* Bump this whenever the policy changes in substance. It is shown to the
   reader, so it must mean something — not the build date. */
const updated = '5 October 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy policy — Blueprint Fitness"
  description="How Blueprint Fitness collects, uses and protects your personal information, and the rights you have over it under UK data protection law."
  current=""
>
  <Schema slot="head" crumbs={[{ name: 'Privacy policy', path: '/privacy/' }]} />
  <section class="section on-dark section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="dim sec-head" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Your data, in plain English</p>
      <h1 class="h-display">Privacy <span class="draft-u">policy</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">What we collect when you enquire, sign up or train with us, what we do
        with it, who else sees it, and how to get it changed or deleted.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;color:var(--sky);font-weight:700">Last updated {updated}</p>
      <div class="onpage reveal">
        <p>On this page</p>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#who">1. Who we are</a></li>
          <li><a href="#what">2. What we collect</a></li>
          <li><a href="#why">3. Why we use it</a></li>
          <li><a href="#sharing">4. Who else sees it</a></li>
          <li><a href="#cookies">5. Cookies and tracking</a></li>
          <li><a href="#keeping">6. How long we keep it</a></li>
          <li><a href="#rights">7. Your rights</a></li>
          <li><a href="#changes">8. Changes to this policy</a></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="policy">

        <div class="callout">
          <p>This policy covers blueprintfitnessldn.com and the three Blueprint Fitness studios.
            The data controller is <strong>PRS Coaching Ltd</strong>, trading as Blueprint
            Fitness, registered in England &amp; Wales.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="h-2" id="who">1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>Blueprint Fitness is a small group personal training business with three studios in
          East London. PRS Coaching Ltd is responsible for the personal information described
          here.</p>
        <p>For anything about your data &mdash; a question, a correction, or a request to delete
          it &mdash; email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. If it is specific to
          one studio you can email that studio directly:</p>
        <ul>
          {studios.map((s) => (
            <li>{s.name} &mdash; <a href={`mailto:${s.email}`}>{s.email}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h-2" id="what">2. What we collect</h2>

        <h3>2.1 When you get in touch or enquire</h3>
        <p>The forms on this site &mdash; the enquiry form, the 30-Day Kickstart sign-up, the
          nutrition consultation request, the member check-in and the cancellation request
          &mdash; ask for some or all of: your first name, email address, phone number, which
          studio you are interested in, and whatever you write in the message box.</p>

        <h3>2.2 When you become a member</h3>
        <p>We hold the details needed to run your membership: your contact details, your chosen
          membership and start date, your payment details and payment history, your attendance
          and bookings, and the notes your coach keeps on your training.</p>

        <h3>2.3 Health information</h3>
        <p>If you tell us about an injury, a condition or anything else that affects how you
          should train, we record it so your coach can keep you safe. This is health data, which
          the law treats as a special category &mdash; we only use it to deliver your training
          safely, we do not use it for marketing, and we never share it outside the coaching
          team without your permission.</p>

        <h3>2.4 When you use the website</h3>
        <p>Our host keeps standard server logs, which include IP addresses, for security and to
          keep the site running. Our CRM sets an identifier in your browser so that if you
          enquire later we can tell which page or advert brought you here &mdash; see
          <a href="#cookies">section 5</a>.</p>

        <h3>2.5 Photos and video</h3>
        <p>We sometimes photograph or film in the studios for social media and the website. We
          ask first, and you can say no, or change your mind later and ask us to take something
          down.</p>

        <h2 class="h-2" id="why">3. Why we use it</h2>
        <p>Under UK data protection law we need a lawful basis for everything we do with your
          information. Ours are:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>To run your membership</strong> &mdash; taking payment, booking you into
            sessions, programming your training, contacting you about your membership. The basis
            is that we have a contract with you.</li>
          <li><strong>To reply to you</strong> &mdash; answering an enquiry, arranging a taster
            session, following up after you have been in. The basis is our legitimate interest
            in responding to someone who has asked to hear from us.</li>
          <li><strong>To train you safely</strong> &mdash; using the health information you give
            us. The basis is your explicit consent, which you give by telling us, and you can
            withdraw it at any time.</li>
          <li><strong>To send you marketing</strong> &mdash; emails and texts about offers,
            events and the Kickstart. The basis is your consent, and every message has an
            unsubscribe link. Stopping marketing does not affect the emails we have to send you
            about your membership.</li>
          <li><strong>To keep our accounts</strong> &mdash; the basis is our legal obligation to
            retain financial records.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h-2" id="sharing">4. Who else sees it</h2>
        <p>We do not sell your information, and we do not share it for anyone else's marketing.
          We do use these companies to run the business, and they process data on our
          instructions:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>GoHighLevel</strong> &mdash; our CRM. It powers every form on this site,
            stores your contact record, and sends our emails and texts.</li>
          <li><strong>Our payment provider</strong> &mdash; membership payments are taken through
            the sign-up forms. Your card details go straight to the payment provider; we never
            see or store a full card number.</li>
          <li><strong>TeamUp</strong> &mdash; the booking system at South Woodford and
            Leytonstone, which holds your bookings and attendance.</li>
          <li><strong>Google</strong> &mdash; the fonts and the studio maps on this site are
            served by Google, so Google receives your IP address when a page loads.</li>
          <li><strong>YouTube</strong> &mdash; the nutrition videos in the members' area are
            hosted on YouTube in its no-cookie mode, so nothing is set unless you press play.</li>
          <li><strong>GitHub</strong> &mdash; hosts this website.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you message us on WhatsApp, that conversation is on Meta's platform and subject to
          their privacy policy as well as ours.</p>
        <p>We will also share information where the law requires it &mdash; for example with HMRC,
          or if we are ever obliged to by a court.</p>
        <p>Some of these companies are based outside the UK. Where that is the case, the transfer
          is covered by the safeguards UK data protection law requires.</p>

        <h2 class="h-2" id="cookies">5. Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>This site does not use advertising cookies and there is no analytics suite tracking
          you around it. Two things do store something in your browser:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Our CRM's tracking script</strong>, which runs on every page and sets an
            identifier so that an enquiry can be matched to the page or advert you arrived
            from.</li>
          <li><strong>Embedded content</strong> &mdash; the Google Maps on the studio pages, and
            the YouTube videos in the members' area if you play one. These set their own cookies,
            which are governed by Google's privacy policy rather than this one.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Doing so will not stop you
          using the site, though the maps and videos may not work.</p>

        <h2 class="h-2" id="keeping">6. How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Enquiries that do not become memberships</strong> &mdash; kept for up to
            24 months, then deleted.</li>
          <li><strong>Member records</strong> &mdash; kept while you are a member and for 24
            months afterwards, so that rejoining is simple.</li>
          <li><strong>Financial records</strong> &mdash; kept for six years after the end of the
            relevant tax year, because we are legally required to.</li>
          <li><strong>Health information</strong> &mdash; deleted when you stop training with us,
            unless you ask us to keep it for a future return.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>You can ask us to delete your information sooner than any of the above, and we will
          unless the law requires us to keep it.</p>

        <h2 class="h-2" id="rights">7. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under UK GDPR you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>ask for a copy of the information we hold about you;</li>
          <li>have anything inaccurate corrected;</li>
          <li>have your information deleted;</li>
          <li>object to how we are using it, or ask us to restrict its use;</li>
          <li>withdraw consent at any time, for marketing or for anything else you consented
            to;</li>
          <li>ask us to send your information to you or another provider in a portable
            format.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will respond within one
          month. There is no charge.</p>
        <p>If you are not happy with how we have handled your information, you can complain to
          the Information Commissioner's Office at
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ico.org.uk</a>
          or on 0303 123 1113. We would rather you came to us first so we can put it right.</p>

        <h2 class="h-2" id="changes">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If we change how we use your information we will update this page and change the date
          at the top. If the change is significant we will tell members directly rather than rely
          on you checking.</p>

        <p style="margin-top:2rem"><a href={url('members/terms/')}>Membership terms &amp;
          conditions &rarr;</a></p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
